      "yearLabel": "2026–2027",
      "limitation": "The 2026–2027 pathway totals 180 EC: ten compulsory 6 EC courses in each of Years 1 and 2, 30 EC open study, three selected 6 EC subjects from seven, and a 12 EC thesis. The retained electives are Econometrics III, Machine Learning for Econometrics and Data Science, and Fair, Transparent and Interpretable Machine Learning; they are choices, not universal requirements. There is no formal graduation route. Teaching is English, with Dutch tutorial/expression/exam-answer options in Years 1–2. BSA requires 42 first-year EC, a pass in Calculus/Analysis I OR Analysis II/Mathematical Reasoning AND a pass in Introduction to Data Science OR Statistics. The English diagnostic or refresher gates Data Analysis I. Zero-credit BRIDGE requires attendance at five of six plenaries. Data Science Practical requires a final DSA mark or a Period-1 Econometrics I/Numerical Methods partial mark of at least5.5. Thesis entry requires120EC including minor and at least two passes from Econometrics II, Multivariate Statistics and Data Science Methods. The thesis is individual quantitative research with a paper and poster/presentation, assessed by supervisor and second reader; topics appear in Period4. The current July2027 diploma deadline concerns current final-year students, not the future Fall2026 entrant’s Year3. The minor normally requires90EC; open study has at most6EC level100, at least12EC level300 and no compulsory-course overlap. Prior board approval applies except stated faculty/university/Education-minor exemptions; the Economics university minor is prohibited for EDS. Course manuals may require attendance. Honours is additional and excluded."
